cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Sufficiency Ladder: Sharing AI's Productivity Gains Through Cash-Flow Profit Participation and Voluntary Work Handoff"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "RI"
version: "5.1"
date-released: "2026-10-27"
url: "https://aj-fyc.github.io/sufficiency-ladder/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AJ-FYC/sufficiency-ladder"
license: MIT
abstract: "A proposal for sharing AI's productivity gains with the people doing the work: companies keep a fixed share of added profit after costs, workers receive the rest partly as capital accounts, and people who approach financial sufficiency hand hours to the next person in line. Includes a working paper, an agent-based model, an interactive simulator and a checker that reproduces every model number in the paper."
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - profit sharing
  - working time
  - agent-based model
  - inequality
  - cash-flow taxation
